{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "062P", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A$", "MATH_0002": "$A = \\bigoplus_{d \\geq 0} A_d$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-section-graded}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:381487eb89dbdd17077e5a807e07f5373b1f80c252c334ceb248c05893ba07d7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0b3daef532cfe83ce86bd74b9fe6ce1d4cdbf2994625bb5e19538c29c057117a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn algebraic geometry cones correspond to graded algebras. By our conventions\na graded ring or algebra <MATH_0001> comes with a grading\n<MATH_0002> by the nonnegative integers, see\nAlgebra, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2cc49544f2e85f3767cff7c6d827d63cff977ba19bd30c4d3b217906fa484aed", "unit_id": "tag:062P:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "062P", "placeholders": {"FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_S \\to \\mathcal{A}_0$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{A}_1$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0010": "$$\nC(\\mathcal{A}) = \\underline{\\Spec}_S(\\mathcal{A}).\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\cite[II, (8.3.1)]{EGA}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-cone}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cfcce86d125534dbb050e475b55fd2f2f3334022d1a3794832bdeb8b9aa39257", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1057cdb717dec2642f329041d92985c16afa062b0644a34b03acccb3f2650aff", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent\ngraded <MATH_0003>-algebra. Assume that <MATH_0004>\nis an isomorphism<FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>Often one imposes the assumption that\n<MATH_0005> is generated by <MATH_0006> over <MATH_0007>. We do not\nassume this in order to be consistent with <REF_0001>.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>cone associated to <MATH_0008><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> or the\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>affine cone associated to <MATH_0009><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nis\n<MATH_0010>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ea1ab50337bcc15c2d99b6fa6afdcc341959e332d8f3007b48f2428279038f78", "unit_id": "tag:062Q:statement"}
{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "062P", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\pi_*\\mathcal{O}_{C(\\mathcal{A})} =\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{n \\geq 0} \\mathcal{A}_n\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7fff8bafa5e8483f5daee6c6003a7ad1c1e718d76f769f70f3233ab502e09e6c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ddc3414075cd1585ac6631b887c6dabbca0b636bfcc75d45f38b540d50baeb19", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe cone associated to a graded sheaf of <MATH_0001>-algebras\ncomes with a bit of extra structure. Namely, we obtain a grading\n<MATH_0002>\nThus we can define an abstract cone as follows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:36f3b00965449979ab5d71700159459d36025f228b19286f3baab698952d8b3d", "unit_id": "tag:062P:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "062P", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\pi : C \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\pi_*\\mathcal{O}_C$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0006": "$\\pi_*\\mathcal{O}_C = \\bigoplus\\nolimits_{n \\geq 0} \\mathcal{A}_n$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{A}_0 = \\mathcal{O}_S$", "MATH_0008": "$\\pi : C \\to S$", "MATH_0009": "$\\pi' : C' \\to S$", "MATH_0010": "$f : C \\to C'$", "MATH_0011": "$$\nf^* : \\pi'_*\\mathcal{O}_{C'} \\longrightarrow \\pi_*\\mathcal{O}_C\n$$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-abstract-cone}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:434166c7fe419baee1062354776b972f703c110d87235d0521019104bdecc663", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9a270776cb9c520cda5f1611d5fe852a9cbd1840a8b6dae4fe4cd64c6647a1dc", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>cone <MATH_0002> over <MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is an\naffine morphism of schemes such that <MATH_0004> is endowed with\nthe structure of a graded <MATH_0005>-algebra\n<MATH_0006>\nsuch that <MATH_0007>. A <TEXTITOPEN_0002>morphism of cones<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nfrom <MATH_0008> to <MATH_0009>\nis a morphism <MATH_0010> such that the induced map\n<MATH_0011>\nis compatible with the given gradings.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4a08f1d95ddf8f46ae6480af85b0588bc6251a2cf45cf3b376914f24c65da740", "unit_id": "tag:062R:statement"}
